---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Passive tree', href: '/passive-tree/' },
];
const buttonClass = 'rounded-md border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold hover:border-accent';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Passive tree explorer"
  description="Explore the full Path of Exile 2 passive skill tree: zoom in, search for any stat, read every node in plain English and plan your points from your class's starting spot."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    <div data-pagefind-body>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Passive tree explorer</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg text-muted">
        This is the whole Path of Exile 2 passive tree. You get one point per level (plus a few from quests), and every
        point unlocks one node next to something you already have. Pick your class to see where you start, then search
        for the stats your build wants.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div data-tree class="mt-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3">
        <label class="flex flex-col text-sm font-semibold">
          Class
          <select data-class class="mt-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface px-2 py-1.5 font-normal"></select>
        </label>
        <label class="flex min-w-48 flex-1 flex-col text-sm font-semibold">
          Search nodes
          <input
            data-search
            type="search"
            placeholder="Try “minion”, “block” or “fire”"
            class="mt-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface px-2 py-1.5 font-normal"
          />
        </label>
        <button type="button" data-next class={buttonClass}>Next match</button>
        <span data-search-count class="self-center text-sm text-muted" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_18rem]">
        <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border">
          <canvas
            class="block h-[65vh] min-h-96 w-full cursor-grab touch-none"
            aria-label="Interactive passive skill tree. Use the search box and the node panel for a text view."
          ></canvas>
          <p data-status class="absolute inset-0 grid place-items-center text-muted">Loading the passive tree…</p>
          <div class="absolute right-2 top-2 flex gap-1">
            <button type="button" data-zoom-in class={buttonClass} aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
            <button type="button" data-zoom-out class={buttonClass} aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
            <button type="button" data-fit class={buttonClass}>Fit</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-muted">Points used</p>
            <p class="text-3xl font-bold" data-points aria-live="polite">0</p>
            <div class="mt-2 flex gap-2">
              <button type="button" data-reset class={buttonClass}>Reset</button>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted">The page address updates as you plan, so you can copy it to share your tree.</p>
          </div>
          <div data-panel class="min-h-40 rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-4" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 grid max-w-5xl gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">How to use it</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Mouse:</strong> drag to move, scroll to zoom, click a node to take it (and the cheapest path to it). Click it again to give it back.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Touch:</strong> drag to move, pinch to zoom, tap a node to read it, then use the button in the panel.</li>
          <li>Names appear once you zoom in. Search highlights every node whose name or stats match.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">What the shapes mean</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Small dots:</strong> small passives with a minor bonus.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Hollow dots:</strong> attribute nodes. You pick Strength, Dexterity or Intelligence.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Large dots:</strong> notables, the strong nodes builds path towards.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Large diamonds:</strong> keystones, which change how your character works, often with a downside.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Small hollow diamonds:</strong> jewel sockets.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-fg">Rings:</strong> class starting spots.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <Callout type="beginner">
        <p>
          You don't need to plan all of this before you play. While levelling, follow your build guide's tree or grab
          notables that boost your main skill and your life. Refunding points later costs gold and nothing else.
        </p>
      </Callout>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">
        Tree data comes from Grinding Gear Games' official <a class="text-accent underline" href="https://github.com/grindinggear/poe2-skilltree-export">passive tree export</a>
        (version 0.5.2). Ascendancy nodes aren't shown yet. For full build planning with gear and skills, use
        <a class="text-accent underline" href="https://pathofbuilding.community/">Path of Building</a>. The node shapes and
        colours are our own, not the game's artwork.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { initPassiveTree } from '../scripts/passive-tree';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-tree]');
  if (root) initPassiveTree(root);
</script>
